In the test file, each case is generated by `_build_case(case_id)`, which computes a `missing` list and returns `len(missing)` as `expected_missing_count`. In `type_check_config_vars`, `missing_vars` is initialized to `[]`, then the loop over `(stdout + stderr).split("\n")` appends one item for every line containing `"is not present at runtime"`, so the final `len(missing_vars)` matches the count of generated missing entries for that case. Evaluating all 15 generated cases gives counts spanning from 0 at the low end to 6 at the high end.

## Answer
{"variable":"len(missing_vars)","min_value":0,"max_value":6}
